# Build output. Nothing under it is ever tracked.
/target

# What a local `cargo mutants` writes beside the tree, #63. It is a run's own
# working output, and the verdict is the run's exit status rather than anything
# left in here.
#
# Both names, because a second run renames the first run's directory rather than
# overwriting it. Ignoring only the first name leaves the rotated copy tracked,
# which is thirty thousand lines of a tool's logs arriving in a commit nobody
# meant to make.
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old
